WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.416
- [Narrator] Cars today can
be controlled from an app.

00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:04.870
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.810
- [Narrator] Their AI assistant

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.920
can help you find the best routes.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.090
Some even have cameras

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.800
that detect whether
you're too tired to drive.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.930
Those high-tech features also mean cars

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.480
are gathering a lot of data about us.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.630
Vehicles can collect up to
several terabytes per hour,

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.490
which can be used to train algorithms

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.200
and help innovation.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.760
In China, that's caught
the government's attention.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.870
They realized data has national security,

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.170
as well as economic attributes.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.100
They need to have their hands on them.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.340
- [Narrator] So after it
announced strict data regulations

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.480
on e-commerce and other tech companies,

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.670
prompting a sell-off of many
Chinese stocks this summer,

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.380
China's setting new rules
for the auto industry.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.720
This time, it's directly
affecting foreign car makers,

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.410
Tesla in particular.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.200
- Tesla will work with
national authorities

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.630
in all countries to ensure data security

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.580
of intelligent and connected vehicles.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.660
- If you're a foreign company in China,

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.249
you increasingly need
to walk a high wire act.

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:03.040
- [Narrator] Tesla and
others will be required

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.610
to store a lot of data,

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.290
for example, about traffic flow

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.610
and charging stations inside China.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.800
Some automakers, including Tesla,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.660
have said they're prepared to do that.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.720
But cybersecurity analysts say authorities

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.070
could now also ask companies
to share that user data,

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.720
changing the game in the
world's largest auto market.

00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:22.657
- And I'm very confident

00:01:22.657 --> 00:01:24.940
that the future in
China is gonna be great.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.530
- [Narrator] For many global car brands,

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.890
China's been the most
important growth market

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.080
in recent years.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.300
Last year alone,

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.567
more than 130,000 Model
3s were sold there.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:37.930
That's more than 1/3 of
global sales for that model.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.330
And Elon Musk is determined
to expand further.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:42.163
China, I think long term

00:01:42.163 --> 00:01:44.000
will be our biggest market,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.090
both where we make the
most number of vehicles

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.510
and where we have the
most number of customers.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.860
- [Narrator] But auto analysts point out

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.860
that those growth opportunities hinge

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.310
on the government's goodwill.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.787
- Want to very much say
thank you and appreciation

00:01:56.787 --> 00:01:58.937
for the Shanghai government
and their support.

00:01:58.937 --> 00:02:01.400
- [Narrator] And Tesla
is particularly exposed.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.600
The American company's cars
rely a lot on software,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.220
and its Model 3 was the
best-selling EV in China last year.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.420
China has already
restricted military staff

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.740
and employees of key state-owned companies

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.250
from using Tesla cars
for fear of data leaks,

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.330
according to people
familiar with the matter.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.350
Tesla declined to comment.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.410
- In the past few months,

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.020
we've essentially seen a regulatory storm.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:24.900
- [Narrator] Samm Sacks is a senior fellow

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.110
at Yale Law School.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.500
She's been researching
China's cybersecurity policy

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.740
for about a decade.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.700
- Foreign automakers, they're
gonna have to walk this dance

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.970
between Beijing and D.C.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.250
And it's a high wire act navigating

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.740
between pressure from Washington

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.500
around decoupling with China,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.743
as well as increased
pressure from Beijing.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.350
- [Narrator] As tensions
between China and the US

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.830
have grown in recent years,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.500
companies handling data have been caught

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.920
in the crosshairs.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.900
In the US, tech firms,
including TikTok and Huawei

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.060
have been targeted by government measures,

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.191
while in China.

00:02:56.191 --> 00:02:59.470
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.390
- [Narrator] Officials have stopped

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.390
what was supposed to be
the world's biggest IPO

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.210
by FinTech giant Ant.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.670
And they've also stepped up
control of tech companies,

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.030
including social media
conglomerate Tencent

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.409
and ride hauling giant DiDi.

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:15.128
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:15.990
- [Narrator] DiDi was investigated

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.560
for national security concerns
shortly after it listed

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.800
in New York, sinking the
company's stock value.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.980
DiDi said it would fully
cooperate with the review.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.260
- They fall under this broader umbrella

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.490
of the party tightening control.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.390
The party is trying to
make the private sector

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.133
better aligned and carry out its vision.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.810
- [Narrator] So what do
international car companies

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.440
have to do after October 1st

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.620
when these rules go into effect?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.210
Tesla said it's set up
data centers in China

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:46.280
to store locally all data
generated by vehicles there.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.630
- These new auto data rules

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.340
are a game changer because it says look,

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.090
the operating environment is changing.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:53.940
- [Narrator] While the requirements

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.090
aren't really a surprise

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.570
since China laid out plans
to increase control of data

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.970
in a 2017 cybersecurity law,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.510
analysts say from now on,

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.300
companies like Tesla could be
asked to share private data

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.620
with local authorities.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.610
- Once foreign car makers
move to store data locally,

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.835
they lost a lot of control.

00:04:10.835 --> 00:04:14.010
Yes, companies very often do push back

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:15.540
on demands by the Chinese government

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.070
to access the data,

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.840
but the space to do
that has been shrinking.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.160
I think in part because of
the spate of new regulations

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.720
that show the government
is prioritizing this data

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.520
as very sensitive to national security.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.353
- [Narrator] And the definition

00:04:29.353 --> 00:04:31.160
of national security's broad.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.450
According to the new rules,

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.170
any information regarding military

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.770
and government locations,
and logistics data,

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.960
traffic or charging stations
for electric vehicles,

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.010
for example, is deemed sensitive,

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.760
and analysts say could be
requested by the government.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.870
China's cybersecurity
authority didn't respond

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.850
to our request seeking comment.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.780
Tesla also didn't respond to our questions

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.800
about how it would handle

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.950
any such requests from authorities.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.740
Elon Musk recently said his company

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.268
would address data security concerns.

00:04:57.268 --> 00:04:58.921
- Data security is not
only the responsibility

00:04:58.921 --> 00:05:00.796
of a single company

00:05:00.796 --> 00:05:02.998
but also the cornerstone

00:05:02.998 --> 00:05:05.134
of the whole industry development.

00:05:05.134 --> 00:05:07.030
- [Narrator] We also asked
several foreign car makers,

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.000
including Ford, BMW, and others

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.480
how they would handle such requests

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.680
but they didn't respond.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:13.930
Tighter rules in China

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.690
are also expected to
affect how companies work.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.650
Remember those algorithms that
improve your car's features?

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.060
They may be harder to develop
for foreign automakers

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.840
if data collected in China
has to stay in China,

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.400
and can't be easily transferred

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.760
to research and development
centers around the world.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.972
- If data to be transferred
outside of China,

00:05:31.972 --> 00:05:33.700
then it has to go

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:38.250
through a very specific
security check process.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.182
- [Narrator] Xiameng Lu
researches data governance.

00:05:40.182 --> 00:05:42.070
She says separating data

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.680
for single countries means
companies may end up working

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.450
on some technologies twice,

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.100
or in parallel in two different places.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.950
- This is a major challenge
to their business model.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.560
This is very costly.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.280
This is not economical.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.780
This is the opposite of
the most economical model.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.080
- [Narrator] Tesla and other automakers

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.390
didn't respond to our questions

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:05.540
about whether this
would impact innovation.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.768
So far, investors have largely
shrugged off the changes.

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:12.260
As Beijing's new rules come into effect,

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.520
stocks of Tesla, Daimler
and other automakers popular

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.430
in China have actually done pretty well

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.430
as demand recovers from its
lows during the pandemic.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.163
In part, that's because the data affected

00:06:22.163 --> 00:06:25.030
by changes in China
only represents one part

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.740
of foreign automakers' overall business.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.280
And industry analysts point out

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.300
that the Chinese market
is simply too important

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.440
for many companies not to comply.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.870
- This is a bellwether of what's to come.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.660
If you're a company and
you're not in the auto sector,

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.370
but you handle a lot of data,

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:44.800
this regulation is actually
foreshadowing what's to come

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:48.043
across all sectors in the
Chinese digital economy

00:06:48.043 --> 00:06:52.025
in ways that could potentially
impact all companies.

00:06:52.025 --> 00:06:54.356
(pensive music)

